  "_provenance": {
    "authored_by": "CC, 2026-10-10, FOR-250",
    "approved_by": "Andrew, 2026-10-09 and 2026-10-10 — all eight soups, one a week, as four fortnights. Blaine's rulings on FOR-250 carry both picks.",
    "why": "Lisa, 2026-09-21: soup and stew options on the menu for fall and winter. The eight soups shipped in FOR-257's library expansion; this fixture puts them in rotations.",
    "SOURCED": "Every dinner here is an existing meal row. The soup order is the 2026-10-09 ruling's. Each week is one of rotation A's or rotation B's own weeks with one dinner swapped for the soup.",
    "DECIDED_BY_CC": "Which dinner each soup replaces, and that every fortnight is rotation A's week 1 followed by rotation B's week 2. See _shape.",
    "adds_no_meal": "This fixture has no fuel_meals_new, and the generator refuses one here."
  },
  "_shape": {
    "why_a_week_1_then_b_week_2_every_time": "A choice, not a necessity. The app reads which rotation a plan ran from the picks that belong to ONE rotation alone (rotationOf), and starts the next cycle from the rotation not just run. Every A or B dinner used here stops being A's or B's alone. Enumerating all 16 ways to draw the four fortnights from A and B, and all 64 legal choices of replaced dinner in each: strict alternation (A1+B2, B1+A2, A1+B2, B1+A2) never keeps both A and B recognisable. Four patterns do. This one keeps four dinners that are rotation A's alone and one that is rotation B's. The one with more variety (the second fortnight drawn from B's week 1 and A's week 2, 11 distinct dinners instead of 8) keeps one each, so a rotation A with its turkey burgers swapped out would read as no rotation and the next cycle would start from A again. Rotation A is the one that matters: a misread B still lands on A next.",
    "not_used_anywhere_here": [
      "garlic-herb-thighs",
      "turkey-burgers",
      "blackened-cod",
      "soy-ginger-stirfry",
      "miso-ginger-salmon"
    ],
    "fish_night_is_never_replaced": true,
    "a_turkey_soup_replaces_that_weeks_turkey_night": [
      "italian-wedding-soup",
      "turkey-chili"
    ]
  },
